  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C+V-(N+C) & =C+V-N-C \\\\  & =\\cancel{C}+V-N-\\cancel{C} \\\\  & =V-N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V-N & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5-1 & 3-(-7) \\\\ 6-2 & -4-(-6) \\\\ -1-3 & -8-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
